{"name":"Parma Plum Red","hex":"#5e3958","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"parma","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dish cooked in the parmigiana style."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small shield carried by the infantry and cavalry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/parma"},{"term":"plum","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fruit and its tree.\n An edible, fleshy stone fruit of species Prunus domestica (European plum) and Prunus americana American plum, often of a dark red or purple colour. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\nA stone-fruit tree which bears this fruit, Prunus domestica. \nThe edible, fleshy stone fruit of several species resembling the plum, or the tree from which they grow. \nPrunus sect. Prunus\nPrunus cerasifera (cherry plum or myrobalan).\nPrunus salicina (Chinese plum or Japanese plum).\nPrunus spinosa (sloe).\nPrunus ursina (bear's plum).\nPrunus sect. Prunocerasus (North American plums)\nPrunus americana (American plum).\nPrunus angustifolia (Chickasaw plum or sand plum).\nPrunus hortulana (hortulan plum).\nPrunus nigra (Canadian plum or black plum).\nPrunus rivularis (creek plum or hog plum).\nPrunus subcordata (Klamath plum or Oregon plum).\nPrunus sect. Armeniaca (better known as apricots)\nPrunus mume, an Asian fruit more closely related to the apricot than the plum, usually consumed pickled, dried, or as a juice or wine; ume.\n A dried grape or raisin, as used in a pudding or cake.","An edible, fleshy stone fruit of species Prunus domestica (European plum) and Prunus americana American plum, often of a dark red or purple colour. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark bluish-red colour.","Choice; especially lavish or preferred."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plum"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Parma","blocks":[{"text":"Parma is a city in the region of Emilia-Romagna in northern Italy, known for its architecture, music, art, prosciutto (ham), cheese and surrounding countryside. With a population of 199,450 as of 2026, Parma is the second most populous city in Emilia-Romagna after Bologna, the region's capital."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Parma_dal_Duomo%2C_settembre_2014-1_%2815481932581%29.jpg/330px-Parma_dal_Duomo%2C_settembre_2014-1_%2815481932581%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parma","wikidata":"Q2683"},{"title":"Plum","blocks":[{"text":"A plum is a fruit of some species in Prunus subg. Prunus. Dried plums are usually called prunes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Plums_African_Rose_-_whole%2C_halved_and_slice.jpg/330px-Plums_African_Rose_-_whole%2C_halved_and_slice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plum","wikidata":"Q12372598"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"},{"title":"Plum (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Plum is a purple color with a brownish-gray tinge, like that shown on the right, or a reddish purple, which is a close representation of the average color of the plum fruit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Plum_on_tree02.jpg/330px-Plum_on_tree02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plum_(color)","wikidata":"Q3108722"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Battistero_di_Parma_-_Vista_Ingresso.jpg/500px-Battistero_di_Parma_-_Vista_Ingresso.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Battistero_di_Parma_-_Vista_Ingresso.jpg/1280px-Battistero_di_Parma_-_Vista_Ingresso.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Battistero_di_Parma_-_Vista_Ingresso.jpg/500px-Battistero_di_Parma_-_Vista_Ingresso.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Baptistery of Parma, 1196–1270","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABattistero_di_Parma_-_Vista_Ingresso.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Parma_nel_XV_secolo.jpg/500px-Parma_nel_XV_secolo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Parma_nel_XV_secolo.jpg/500px-Parma_nel_XV_secolo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna